{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The rubber grommets fit my wire connector purchases because they would help protect wiring where it passes through holes.",
    "The general-purpose epoxy fits my history of strong tape and vinyl cement purchases because it offers another practical way to repair things made from different materials."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Marine epoxy and refrigeration sealant assume specific repair jobs that my adhesive and clamp purchases do not establish.",
    "Feeler gauges, cutting wheels and precision tweezers require tasks I have not shown a need for, while the safety can addresses a storage need I do not currently have.",
    "The locking nuts and electronic cleaner could be useful someday, but I would need known bolt sizes or an actual contact-cleaning problem before choosing them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair-supply purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop tool, even when its purpose is quite different.",
    "Wire connectors and hose clamps seem to have been stretched into assumptions about delicate electronics work and refrigeration repairs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A clear practical connection matters to me: grommets complement wiring supplies, whereas precision tweezers serve a separate task.",
    "I distinguish broadly useful repair supplies from specialized products that I would buy only for a particular problem."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical repair interests but often assumed specialized projects without enough evidence."
}"}
